      "locator": "FSRA guidance PE0196INF (effective January 1, 2021), 'Appendix A: maximum annual income payment amount table for an Ontario LIF or LRIF (Using C/F formula in section 6 of Schedules 1, 1.1 and 2 to the Regulation)', column 'Maximum payment as a percentage of the LIF or LRIF balance at start of fiscal year', every row, ages 41 to 90 (age 41 = 5.98531%, age 90 = 100.00000%). The page says the table holds for any year unless the November CANSIM V122487 rate (long-term Government of Canada bond rate) exceeds 6.00%; F uses 6.00% (greater of CANSIM V122487 and 6.00%) for the first 15 years and 6.00% thereafter. The page also says the maximum is the greater of the C/F amount and the previous fiscal year's investment earnings, including unrealized gains or losses (for a Post-2008 LIF after a transfer from another LIF or LRIF, the greatest of those and the transferring fund's plus receiving LIF's previous-year earnings). Percentages are prorated for a first fiscal year shorter than 12 months. The value holds only the table."
